WEBVTT

00:01.208 --> 00:04.384
♪ it seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.453 --> 00:07.730
♪ is violence in movies
and sex on tv ♪

00:07.798 --> 00:10.873
♪ but where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.942 --> 00:13.850
♪ on which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.917 --> 00:17.797
♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.865 --> 00:20.672
♪ lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.740 --> 00:22.278
♪ all the things that make us ♪

00:22.346 --> 00:24.018
♪ laugh and cry ♪

00:24.086 --> 00:26.895
♪ he's... A...
Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.770 --> 00:36.443
Hi, chris.

00:36.511 --> 00:38.047
How'd you do on
your science test?

00:38.115 --> 00:39.285
I got a "d."

00:39.353 --> 00:41.326
A "d"? That's fantastic!

00:41.393 --> 00:43.165
Just kiddin'.
I know it means you suck.

00:43.233 --> 00:45.071
Come here,
you delightful idiot.

00:45.140 --> 00:46.443
Another "d," chris?

00:46.511 --> 00:49.253
I'm sorry, mom,
but science is so hard.

00:49.319 --> 00:51.292
Well, maybe you just need
a little extra help.

00:51.360 --> 00:53.266
Dad, would you help me
with my homework?

00:53.333 --> 00:55.172
Uh, chris, I've got to
tell you, that sounds worse

00:55.239 --> 00:56.778
Than a trip to
a failing mall.

00:58.083 --> 00:59.321
All right, kids,
your mom is

00:59.389 --> 01:01.227
Going to go to the cinnabon
that has the cage

01:01.295 --> 01:02.897
Pulled halfway down,
and I'm going to go

01:02.966 --> 01:05.406
To the stereo store next
to the dead fountain
with garbage in it.

01:05.473 --> 01:07.647
Let's say we meet back here
under the glue outline

01:07.714 --> 01:09.321
Of the old limited sign.

01:09.388 --> 01:11.024
Well, it doesn't
matter anyway.

01:11.093 --> 01:13.199
Every time I try to study,
the evil monkey

01:13.267 --> 01:15.106
Comes out of my closet
and scares me.

01:19.690 --> 01:22.231
Oh, for god's sake, chris,
you're in high school now.

01:22.299 --> 01:24.170
Stop talking about
that evil monkey.

01:24.238 --> 01:25.240
He's not real.

01:25.308 --> 01:26.578
He is too real!

01:26.647 --> 01:27.782
I can prove it!

01:27.850 --> 01:29.154
Well, you'll have to
do a better job

01:29.222 --> 01:30.691
Than you did on
your science test.

01:30.759 --> 01:32.499
Or than god did
when he left the iron

01:32.565 --> 01:34.171
On ellen barkin's
face too long.

01:35.977 --> 01:37.013
Oh, damn.

01:37.081 --> 01:38.719
How is it?
You know what?

01:38.788 --> 01:40.491
We'll put you in the '80s.
You'll pass for hot.

01:40.559 --> 01:41.797
Now get in the van
with kelly mcgillis.

01:43.034 --> 01:46.143
Next stop: Hollywood!

01:46.211 --> 01:48.517
(braying)

01:51.999 --> 01:54.539
<i>Tv announcer:
Up next, the hannah montana
marathon.</i>

01:54.607 --> 01:56.680
Yes!
And for all you fans,

01:56.747 --> 01:59.354
The miley cyrus tour is coming
to the quahog civic center

01:59.423 --> 02:00.626
For three nights only.

02:00.695 --> 02:02.333
Call to get your tickets now!

02:02.401 --> 02:04.406
Oh! Oh, my god! Oh, my god!
Oh, my god!

02:04.472 --> 02:06.045
But not now,
'cause it just sold out.

02:06.113 --> 02:07.885
What? Oh, no! No!
No, no! No!

02:07.952 --> 02:09.489
I'm calling anyway!

02:09.557 --> 02:11.462
<i>I need hannah montana tickets
and I need them now!</i>

02:11.531 --> 02:13.970
Never mind who this is!
Can you get them or not?

02:14.038 --> 02:15.911
I guess I should dial
something first.

02:15.979 --> 02:17.919
What's all the noise?
What are you watching?

02:17.985 --> 02:19.723
Sorry, but you
know the rules.

02:19.792 --> 02:21.596
Hannah can't do
the photo shoot

02:21.664 --> 02:23.838
Until miley
finishes her homework.

02:23.905 --> 02:25.176
You can't tell
hannah what to do.

02:25.245 --> 02:26.481
She's not your daughter.

02:26.548 --> 02:29.222
Wait, so miley's my daughter,
but hannah isn't?

02:29.289 --> 02:30.930
Right.
Great.

02:30.998 --> 02:31.998
Put your wig on.

02:32.067 --> 02:33.472
(audience laughter sound effect)

02:33.540 --> 02:35.712
Shut up!
This is real.

02:35.779 --> 02:38.320
<i>Ha! You're watching
hannah montana?</i>

02:38.388 --> 02:40.260
Well, yeah.
To make fun of it.

02:40.328 --> 02:42.735
I mean, look how stupid
she is with her clothes

02:42.802 --> 02:45.076
And her makeup
and, and-and, and,

02:45.143 --> 02:47.451
And that fabulous hair
and, oh, my god!

02:47.520 --> 02:49.860
Brian, it's my favorite show!
It's my favorite show ever!

02:49.928 --> 02:51.198
Gay.
And she's coming to town

02:51.265 --> 02:52.603
And I have to get
tickets, brian.

02:52.671 --> 02:54.341
You have to help me
get tickets!
No.

02:54.409 --> 02:56.682
It's a stupid show
and a huge waste of time.

02:56.750 --> 03:00.494
(voice breaking):
But... She's my favorite.

03:00.563 --> 03:02.804
Oh, my god, are you...
Are you crying?

03:02.871 --> 03:05.144
(crying): Yes!
Hannah montana is my hero!

03:05.212 --> 03:06.651
I love her so, so much.

03:06.717 --> 03:08.924
And this is the only time
she's gonna be in town

03:08.993 --> 03:10.529
And now I'll never
get to see her!

03:10.596 --> 03:12.335
Will you help me?

03:12.403 --> 03:14.075
(sighs)
all right, fine.

03:17.921 --> 03:19.327
Hey, chris.

03:19.395 --> 03:21.701
You want to practice
kissing again?
I'm busy.

03:21.769 --> 03:24.175
I set up a video camera
last night so I can prove

03:24.244 --> 03:26.317
To mom and dad that
the evil monkey is real,

03:26.384 --> 03:27.787
And I want to see
what I got.

03:44.979 --> 03:46.216
(tape squeals
while fast-forwarding)

03:59.094 --> 04:00.931
(fast-forwarding)

04:05.116 --> 04:07.154
Huh. Nothin'.

04:07.221 --> 04:10.030
All right, it's time
to play rough.

04:29.832 --> 04:32.740
I got you, you bastard!

04:34.882 --> 04:37.221
Well, here he is.

04:37.290 --> 04:39.127
The evil monkey!

04:39.195 --> 04:40.734
Do you believe me now?!

04:40.803 --> 04:42.139
Holy crap!

04:42.205 --> 04:43.444
It is real!

04:43.511 --> 04:46.286
Oh, my god!
I thought I was the only one.

04:46.354 --> 04:48.293
Meg, we're do--
we're doin'...

04:48.361 --> 04:49.664
We're doin'
chris' monkey.

04:55.047 --> 04:57.288
Oh, my god,
chris was right!

04:57.357 --> 04:59.394
Holy crap, chris,
is that thing dangerous?

04:59.462 --> 05:01.269
Yes, he's evil!

05:01.336 --> 05:02.639
I'm not really evil.

05:02.708 --> 05:03.910
(gasps)
it talks!

05:03.979 --> 05:05.349
If-if someone will
please untie me,

05:05.417 --> 05:06.820
I'll explain everything.

05:06.888 --> 05:08.126
No, dad,
don't do it!

05:08.194 --> 05:09.328
He's evil!

05:09.397 --> 05:10.600
Look, just trust me.

05:10.669 --> 05:12.641
This is all a huge
misunderstanding.

05:12.708 --> 05:15.081
Chris, I think we
should give him a chance
to explain himself.

05:15.150 --> 05:16.454
No!

05:18.092 --> 05:19.729
(sighs)
thank you very much.

05:19.797 --> 05:21.370
Now, I know this looks bad,

05:21.438 --> 05:23.108
Me living in your
son's closet and all,

05:23.176 --> 05:25.516
But it's a very
complex situation.

05:25.583 --> 05:28.192
You see, basically, I got home
from work one day,

05:28.260 --> 05:30.834
And found my wife cheating on me
with another monkey.

05:30.903 --> 05:32.606
Oh, that's terrible.

05:32.675 --> 05:35.082
I fell into a deep depression
after the divorce,

05:35.149 --> 05:36.756
Which ended up
costing me my job.

05:36.824 --> 05:39.197
All my money was gone,
which means I lost the house.

05:39.264 --> 05:40.534
So, I moved into
chris' closet,

05:40.603 --> 05:42.373
Just until I got
back on my feet again.

05:42.441 --> 05:44.815
Wound up living in there
for nine years.

05:44.883 --> 05:47.390
Oh, my god,
you've missed so much!

05:47.458 --> 05:48.897
Like when america
was attacked

05:48.965 --> 05:51.137
By mentally challenged
suicide bombers.

05:51.204 --> 05:52.709
<i>Allahu akbar!</i>

05:54.181 --> 05:55.450
You know something?

05:55.518 --> 05:57.323
You're not evil
at all, are you?

05:57.391 --> 05:58.796
No, he's not.

05:58.864 --> 06:00.970
He's just a poor fellow
who's down on his luck.

06:01.038 --> 06:02.408
Easy for you to say!

06:02.476 --> 06:05.285
He doesn't hide in your
closet making a scary face!

06:05.352 --> 06:07.057
That's just the face
I make when I'm thinking.

06:07.125 --> 06:08.495
And you're always
pointing at me!

06:08.563 --> 06:10.235
I was trying to start
a conversation.

06:10.303 --> 06:11.940
And you do that weird
trembling thing!

06:12.007 --> 06:13.244
I have a copper deficiency.

06:13.312 --> 06:15.252
Look, chris, I'm sorry
if I scared you before,

06:15.320 --> 06:17.659
But this is a great chance
for us to start over.

06:17.727 --> 06:19.130
No, it isn't!

06:19.198 --> 06:21.640
You can fool everyone else,
but you can't fool me!

06:21.707 --> 06:22.743
You go to hell!

06:37.864 --> 06:40.871
(indistinct conversations)

06:46.356 --> 06:47.728
(gasps)

06:47.796 --> 06:50.605
(indistinct conversation)

06:50.673 --> 06:52.276
Okay, now remember
to play it cool.

06:52.345 --> 06:54.083
Act like you belong here.

06:54.150 --> 06:56.324
Oh, my god, miley!
I love you! I love you!

06:56.392 --> 06:57.494
I love you!
I'm your biggest fan!

06:57.562 --> 06:59.099
Can I touch your hair?!
(screams)

06:59.167 --> 07:00.103
Who are you guys?

07:00.171 --> 07:01.441
How did you get back here?

07:01.509 --> 07:02.845
Look, I'm really
sorry about this.

07:02.912 --> 07:04.451
This is my friend stewie.

07:04.519 --> 07:07.763
H-he's just a baby and
he's your biggest fan and...

07:07.830 --> 07:08.999
He has cancer.

07:09.068 --> 07:10.839
Oh, my god! Really?

07:10.907 --> 07:12.477
Yeah, he's got
a tumor in his head

07:12.546 --> 07:14.853
The size of a football.
I think I can see it.

07:14.920 --> 07:16.257
Well, in that case,

07:16.324 --> 07:18.298
I wouldn't feel right
about throwing you out.

07:18.366 --> 07:20.237
Especially if you're
my biggest fan.

07:20.305 --> 07:21.708
(shudders happily)

07:24.653 --> 07:27.361
I mean, sarah silverman
is just one of the most

07:27.429 --> 07:29.168
Wonderful people
you'll ever meet.

07:29.236 --> 07:30.740
Oh, that's so
good to hear.

07:30.808 --> 07:32.879
I want to like her.
She's so funny.

07:32.948 --> 07:34.652
I want her
to also be nice.

07:34.720 --> 07:37.697
Well, I'm glad you guys are
having such a great time

07:37.764 --> 07:40.807
With that evil thing
that tortured me for years!

07:40.876 --> 07:43.582
Dad, I thought you
were going to help me
with my book report.

07:43.650 --> 07:45.924
Chris, there is
a monkey here.

07:45.993 --> 07:48.299
And I just fed him a whole
bag of subway sandwiches.

07:48.367 --> 07:50.339
In a couple hours,
we are going to sit around

07:50.408 --> 07:52.647
And throw his soft bread stool
at each other.

07:52.714 --> 07:54.620
Now, you are welcome
to be a part of that.

07:54.688 --> 07:56.026
Or not.

07:56.093 --> 07:58.099
I'm just telling you
what's gonna happen.

07:58.167 --> 08:00.372
Well, thanks for
nothing, dad!

08:01.881 --> 08:03.282
Don't mind him, monkey.

08:03.350 --> 08:05.188
He's just a big
disappointment.

08:05.256 --> 08:07.698
Like things that look
like dvds from far away.

08:07.764 --> 08:09.438
(gasps):
Dvds!

08:09.506 --> 08:10.573
Aw, books.

08:24.990 --> 08:26.360
(keys clacking)

08:29.572 --> 08:31.613
(scratching)

08:31.680 --> 08:33.919
Ah... That feels so good.

08:33.988 --> 08:35.391
You are an artist.

08:35.459 --> 08:36.697
Thank you.

08:36.764 --> 08:38.703
Lois doesn't like
my toenails

08:38.771 --> 08:40.442
'cause they stab her
in the night.

08:40.509 --> 08:41.746
Hear that, lois?

08:41.815 --> 08:43.585
Somebody likes my toenails.

08:43.653 --> 08:44.789
Good for you, peter.

08:44.858 --> 08:46.529
Good for this family.

08:46.596 --> 08:48.167
Good for all of us.

08:48.235 --> 08:49.607
Mom! Dad!

08:49.675 --> 08:51.679
I got an "a"
on my book report!

08:51.747 --> 08:53.285
That's wonderful, honey!

08:53.352 --> 08:55.460
Congratulations, chris.
What'd you write about?

08:55.527 --> 08:56.897
I, um...

08:56.965 --> 09:00.376
<i>"the slave trade allegory
of curious george."</i>

09:00.445 --> 09:02.383
W-wait a minute, I didn't--
I didn't write this.

09:02.451 --> 09:03.853
Oh, really?

09:03.922 --> 09:06.028
Did... Did you
write this?

09:06.096 --> 09:08.002
Well, I can't take
all the credit.

09:08.070 --> 09:10.376
I've been listening
to you talk in your
sleep for years,

09:10.445 --> 09:12.517
So I just put your
thoughts on paper,
that's all.

09:12.585 --> 09:16.330
Wow, that's the nicest thing
anyone's ever done for me.

09:16.398 --> 09:19.575
Thanks, evil monk--
thanks, monkey.

09:19.642 --> 09:21.781
Ah, I'd get up to hug you,
but sittin' down's

09:21.849 --> 09:23.086
The only thing
keepin' the poop in.

09:23.154 --> 09:24.188
Nah, that's okay.

09:28.070 --> 09:29.908
I can't believe
I'm sitting here

09:29.976 --> 09:31.380
With you, miley cyrus.

09:31.448 --> 09:32.853
It's like I'm in a dream.

09:32.921 --> 09:34.457
Well, that makes
me happy, stewie.

09:34.525 --> 09:35.829
What are you doing?

09:35.898 --> 09:37.567
Oh, I'm just writing
some new lyrics.

09:37.636 --> 09:38.907
Oh, you write
your own lyrics?

09:38.974 --> 09:41.682
Yeah.
So do I...

09:41.750 --> 09:43.589
Oh, you wrote a song?

09:43.657 --> 09:44.759
Look at you.

09:44.826 --> 09:46.599
You're a regular
little tim mcgraw.

09:46.667 --> 09:48.907
(chuckling):
Oh, oh, I'm...

09:48.974 --> 09:51.214
I'm-I'm a little better
than tim mcgraw.

09:51.282 --> 09:53.589
Hey, these are
pretty good, stewie.

09:53.656 --> 09:54.758
Really?

09:54.827 --> 09:56.164
Do you think you
could sing them?

09:56.231 --> 09:57.704
Only if you sing with me.

09:57.771 --> 09:59.308
(squealing):
Ooh! Ooh!

09:59.376 --> 10:01.214
(pop intro begins)

10:03.122 --> 10:05.864
♪ you and I didn't
quite get along ♪

10:05.932 --> 10:08.037
♪ when we first met ♪

10:10.212 --> 10:12.319
♪ when you put us together ♪

10:12.387 --> 10:14.994
♪ we just didn't blend ♪

10:17.302 --> 10:19.377
♪ but the more that I know you ♪

10:19.445 --> 10:21.684
♪ the more it's a good bet ♪

10:24.529 --> 10:26.299
♪ that we've got
what it takes ♪

10:26.368 --> 10:29.176
♪ to be very best friends... ♪

10:31.418 --> 10:34.326
Miley & stewie:
♪ friendship is
the best thing ever ♪

10:34.394 --> 10:36.467
Miley:
♪ except for best friendship ♪

10:36.535 --> 10:38.206
♪ which is a little better ♪

10:38.274 --> 10:40.179
Stewie:
♪ you mean a lot better ♪

10:40.247 --> 10:41.884
Miley:
♪ I mean a lot better ♪

10:41.953 --> 10:43.791
Stewie:
♪ now we're friends ♪

10:43.860 --> 10:46.803
♪ yes it's true
that no one else ♪

10:46.870 --> 10:49.144
♪ can friend me like you ♪

10:51.050 --> 10:54.629
Miley & stewie:
♪ friendship is
the best thing ever ♪

10:54.696 --> 10:58.072
Miley:
♪ except for best friendship
which is a little better ♪

10:58.141 --> 10:59.746
Stewie:
♪ you mean a lot better ♪

10:59.814 --> 11:02.889
Miley:
♪ I mean a lot better... ♪

11:02.958 --> 11:04.662
Miley & stewie:
♪ with you. ♪

11:09.897 --> 11:11.369
Hey, where you guys been?

11:11.436 --> 11:13.442
We went to the
father/son barbecue.

11:13.510 --> 11:16.051
You drove all the way up
to fatherson for a barbecue?

11:16.118 --> 11:19.162
No, dad, it was a barbecue
for fathers and sons.

11:19.230 --> 11:20.867
Wait a minute--
you went with the monkey

11:20.935 --> 11:22.439
To a father/son thing?

11:22.506 --> 11:24.848
Well, it's not like you ever
take me anywhere.

11:24.916 --> 11:26.384
What?
Oh, listen,
peter, I didn't...

11:26.453 --> 11:28.325
Meg, please!
It's true.

11:28.393 --> 11:30.032
You never want to do
anything with me!

11:30.100 --> 11:33.042
But the monkey's been taking me
to all the fun places I like,

11:33.110 --> 11:35.349
<i>And he's been helping me
with all my homework!</i>

11:35.417 --> 11:38.261
He helped me get
an "a" in algebra!

11:38.328 --> 11:40.332
How did the monkey know you
needed help with algebra?

11:40.400 --> 11:42.272
Because he asked!

11:43.445 --> 11:44.813
That's right, dad.

11:44.881 --> 11:46.954
You never ask,
and even if you did,

11:47.023 --> 11:48.461
You never listen!

11:48.529 --> 11:50.098
And now you're getting
mad at the monkey

11:50.167 --> 11:51.837
Because he actually cares?

11:51.906 --> 11:53.711
Screw you!

11:53.779 --> 11:57.089
You are the worst dad
in the world and I hate you!

11:57.158 --> 11:59.297
Well... Well,
I hate you, too!

12:00.468 --> 12:01.806
Ah, damn.

12:01.873 --> 12:04.513
I left my cell phone up
at that monkey/kid barbecue.

12:04.581 --> 12:06.321
I thought you said it was
a father/son barbecue.

12:06.388 --> 12:07.791
Yeah, but it was up
in monkeykid.

12:07.860 --> 12:09.297
What?!

12:21.536 --> 12:24.310
Boy, you guys have been
awful quiet this morning.

12:24.379 --> 12:27.519
Lois, could you ask chris
to pass the maple syrup?

12:27.588 --> 12:29.293
Meg, could you
tell dad

12:29.361 --> 12:31.333
That he's too fat
to need extra syrup?

12:31.402 --> 12:33.609
Lois, could you tell chris
that I'm sorry

12:33.676 --> 12:36.551
I ever planted the seed version
of him in your vagina?

12:36.620 --> 12:38.023
I want you two
to stop this.

12:38.092 --> 12:40.364
This is no way for
a father and son to act.

12:40.433 --> 12:41.970
Well, according to him,
that stupid monkey's

12:42.037 --> 12:43.843
More of a father
to him than I am.

12:43.911 --> 12:46.517
He makes time for me
and you never do.

12:46.585 --> 12:49.728
You're supposed to love me
and all you do is hurt me.

12:49.796 --> 12:51.536
This morning I had
a hard poo that hurt,

12:51.603 --> 12:52.839
But then it felt great.

12:52.906 --> 12:54.613
Meg, I'm trying to be
mad right now,

12:54.681 --> 12:56.083
But that's making
me want to smile.

13:00.801 --> 13:01.937
(laughing)

13:02.005 --> 13:03.877
This'll get chris.

13:03.944 --> 13:06.051
Hey, classmates.

13:06.119 --> 13:07.523
Griffin.
Did you gain weight?

13:07.590 --> 13:08.859
Eh, that's
not important.

13:08.928 --> 13:10.098
But you know
what is important?

13:10.166 --> 13:11.602
I'm gay now.

13:11.671 --> 13:14.144
Let's all of us go be
gay somewhere together.

13:14.213 --> 13:15.750
And then you go
tell all your friends

13:15.817 --> 13:18.159
That I welcome them
to be gay with me, too.

13:18.227 --> 13:20.400
Because I am gay.

13:20.467 --> 13:21.703
I'll be gay with you.

13:21.771 --> 13:24.012
Oh, this is too perfect.

13:24.079 --> 13:26.421
Chris is going to be
so gay by the end of this.

13:30.568 --> 13:31.905
What's this?

13:31.973 --> 13:34.848
"put your head between
these two restrained logs

13:34.916 --> 13:36.419
And win a free hat"?

13:37.759 --> 13:39.129
Well, that's a no-brainer.

13:39.198 --> 13:41.335
Come on, you fat (bleep).

13:41.404 --> 13:42.441
Do it.

13:46.288 --> 13:47.223
(screaming)

13:47.292 --> 13:49.129
(laughing)

13:50.536 --> 13:52.374
Who's laughing now?

13:52.442 --> 13:54.815
I got my hat.

13:58.128 --> 14:00.501
Hey, guys.
I stopped at pinkberry

14:00.569 --> 14:02.007
And I got some
for everybody.

14:02.075 --> 14:03.846
Wow, thanks.
You're welcome.

14:03.914 --> 14:06.188
I've got to go put on my
face for press interviews.

14:06.255 --> 14:08.529
Stewie, can you hand
me my cell phone?
Oh, sure.

14:08.596 --> 14:09.933
(static crackles)

14:10.000 --> 14:11.940
Thanks!

14:12.007 --> 14:13.311
That was weird--
did you hear that

14:13.380 --> 14:14.784
When I was giving
her the phone?

14:14.852 --> 14:17.393
No.
It was like,
interference or something.

14:18.563 --> 14:19.868
Wait a second.

14:27.661 --> 14:30.268
(both gasp)

14:32.978 --> 14:34.816
Oh, my god!

14:34.884 --> 14:36.356
She's an android!

14:36.425 --> 14:38.330
Miley cyrus is an android!

14:38.398 --> 14:39.634
Of course.

14:39.702 --> 14:41.674
She's a product
of disney imagineering.

14:41.741 --> 14:44.183
They built a perfect
robot teen idol.

14:44.250 --> 14:46.289
Yes, assuring that
she could never fail.

14:46.357 --> 14:48.329
Like famous duelist
sir henry

14:48.397 --> 14:50.370
"giant-hole-in-the-torso"
wickenshire.

14:51.909 --> 14:52.945
(gunshot)

14:53.014 --> 14:54.718
Aha!
Right through me!

14:54.785 --> 14:57.693
Prepare for returned fire,
sir joseph broadfront.

14:57.762 --> 15:00.235
I give you one last
chance to rescind

15:00.304 --> 15:02.511
Your insult of calling
me a "common dandy."

15:02.579 --> 15:04.485
Never!

15:09.802 --> 15:12.311
My god, I can't believe
she's an android.

15:12.379 --> 15:14.819
Do you think we should
tell someone or do something?

15:14.887 --> 15:16.358
Well, we could
do something.

15:16.426 --> 15:17.995
Like what?
Well, look at her.

15:18.063 --> 15:20.906
She dances like a real girl.
She moves like a real girl.

15:20.975 --> 15:22.545
Yeah?

15:22.614 --> 15:24.653
Do you think she
does other stuff
like a real girl?

15:24.721 --> 15:26.290
You know, if you
reprogrammed her?

15:26.358 --> 15:27.964
Brian, that's sick!
She's 16!

15:28.032 --> 15:29.369
I'm eight.

15:29.435 --> 15:30.906
All right, I'll see
what I can do.

15:32.077 --> 15:33.448
Hey, miley.

15:33.516 --> 15:34.686
Oh, hi, stewie.

15:34.754 --> 15:36.326
Hey, um, your shirt
tag is showing.

15:36.393 --> 15:37.664
Let me just, uh...

15:40.339 --> 15:41.944
There we go, all done.

15:42.013 --> 15:43.918
(electricity crackling)

15:43.986 --> 15:45.121
Um...

15:46.326 --> 15:48.834
Miley smash!

15:48.902 --> 15:50.773
(roaring)

15:50.841 --> 15:52.180
Uh-oh...
Hang on, hang on.

15:52.247 --> 15:53.348
Maybe I can fix this.

15:54.688 --> 15:56.025
(growling)

15:56.093 --> 15:57.429
Run!

15:59.739 --> 16:01.944
Monkey, do you think
you could help me?

16:02.012 --> 16:03.817
I just can't stand
peter and chris

16:03.885 --> 16:05.390
Being at each other's
throats anymore.

16:05.458 --> 16:07.498
Of course, lois;
I'm sure if we can just

16:07.565 --> 16:08.934
Get them in the same
room together,

16:09.002 --> 16:10.574
I can convince them
to talk it out.

16:10.643 --> 16:12.178
Why don't you invite
peter to lunch,

16:12.247 --> 16:14.522
And I'll invite chris,
and we'll see what we can do.

16:14.588 --> 16:17.263
Oh, thank you.
I really appreciate it.

16:23.185 --> 16:24.555
What the hell
are you doing here?

16:24.623 --> 16:25.859
I thought I was
meeting lois.

16:25.928 --> 16:27.531
She wanted me to
talk to you guys

16:27.599 --> 16:28.969
About the way
you've been behaving.

16:29.037 --> 16:30.978
Look, monkey, chris is
being a jerk, all right?

16:31.045 --> 16:32.547
And there is
nothing you can say

16:32.616 --> 16:34.453
That will make me
change my mind about that.

16:34.522 --> 16:36.128
Peter, you're
acting bananas.

16:36.196 --> 16:38.068
(laughs)
all right, I'll listen.

16:38.134 --> 16:40.475
You're both good guys
and that's why it's important

16:40.544 --> 16:42.146
For you to reconcile
your differences.

16:42.214 --> 16:43.987
Chris, I know you're angry,

16:44.055 --> 16:45.826
But do you really
hate your father?

16:45.894 --> 16:48.334
No, I just think
he's a douche.

16:48.402 --> 16:50.074
Sometimes he is.

16:50.142 --> 16:52.750
And peter, do you
really hate your son?

16:52.816 --> 16:56.060
No, but sometimes he's
such a little fat jerk.

16:56.129 --> 16:58.837
Well, it's only because you
never have any time for me!

16:58.905 --> 17:00.310
Peter, do you think
you could make

17:00.377 --> 17:02.048
A little more time
for your son?

17:02.115 --> 17:04.055
Yeah, I guess so.

17:04.123 --> 17:06.698
(stewie & brian screaming)

17:06.764 --> 17:08.470
What the hell
was that about?

17:08.539 --> 17:10.108
Was that stewie
and brian?

17:10.176 --> 17:11.581
(miley roaring)

17:11.648 --> 17:13.854
(people screaming)

17:13.923 --> 17:14.925
(explosion)

17:16.130 --> 17:17.968
(roaring continues)

17:24.793 --> 17:27.100
(roars)

17:27.167 --> 17:29.006
(gasps)
it's miley cyrus!

17:29.073 --> 17:30.812
And she's
destroying the city!

17:30.880 --> 17:33.520
Oh, my god!

17:33.587 --> 17:35.862
Ms. Cyrus, I ask you
to stop what you're doing.

17:35.931 --> 17:37.836
I don't just mean this,
I mean everything:

17:37.904 --> 17:40.745
The show, the music--
it's all just awful.

17:40.814 --> 17:43.220
(roaring)

17:43.288 --> 17:44.793
(monkey screams)

17:49.276 --> 17:50.778
Dad, we've got
to help him!

17:50.847 --> 17:51.851
Do something!

17:51.918 --> 17:53.187
What am I supposed to do?!

17:53.254 --> 17:55.595
You're my dad!
Think of something!

18:00.880 --> 18:03.154
Quagmire, fire up
the biplane.

18:03.221 --> 18:05.428
My son needs my help.

18:16.734 --> 18:18.574
(roaring)

18:25.731 --> 18:26.935
All right, peter,
we're closing in.

18:27.002 --> 18:28.073
Get ready to fire.

18:29.378 --> 18:32.051
(laughs along with
gun firing)

18:32.119 --> 18:34.393
(giggitys along with
gun firing)

18:37.572 --> 18:39.477
(roaring)

18:45.498 --> 18:47.237
(roaring)

18:51.419 --> 18:53.993
(roars)

19:09.914 --> 19:11.551
(guns firing)

19:24.798 --> 19:26.603
(roaring)

19:40.016 --> 19:41.855
(roaring)

19:45.400 --> 19:47.272
Monkey! Grab my hand!

20:14.666 --> 20:16.002
Well, the airplane got her.

20:16.070 --> 20:18.344
Oh, no, it wasn't the airplane.

20:18.411 --> 20:21.688
'twas beauty
killed the beast.

20:21.756 --> 20:23.094
You know, brian,
here's your shot.

20:23.161 --> 20:24.330
Go for it.

20:25.670 --> 20:27.508
Oop, too late.

20:27.577 --> 20:28.679
No, it's not.

20:32.425 --> 20:34.198
Thanks for everything,
monkey.

20:34.265 --> 20:37.309
You made me realize how much
chris really means to me

20:37.377 --> 20:40.619
And how I should always remember
not to take him for granted.

20:40.687 --> 20:42.393
Well, sometimes
all anybody needs

20:42.461 --> 20:44.064
Is a little bit
of a wake-up call.

20:44.132 --> 20:45.870
And now that you two
are getting along again,

20:45.938 --> 20:47.342
My work here is done.

20:47.410 --> 20:48.946
Guess I'll be
moving on now.

20:49.014 --> 20:50.520
You have to leave?

20:50.588 --> 20:52.057
But I thought
you were gonna go

20:52.125 --> 20:53.831
Back to living
in my closet again.

20:53.898 --> 20:56.039
I think that time of
my life is over, chris.

20:56.107 --> 20:57.241
But I'll always remember you.

21:00.488 --> 21:02.828
But... Where will you go?

21:02.895 --> 21:04.467
I'll go where I'm needed.

21:04.468 --> 21:09.479
Sync by honeybunny

21:11.223 --> 21:13.932
Dad, there's an evil
monkey in my closet!

21:14.000 --> 21:16.474
Tom: I don't care, son.
I just do not care.

21:16.475 --> 22:17.475
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru